dtcalc> # A bare colon literal is a clock reading where that typechecks...
dtcalc> 12:15
2026-05-23T12:15:00-04:00  America/New_York
dtcalc> 12:13 in Tokyo
2026-05-24T01:13:00+09:00  Asia/Tokyo
dtcalc> # ...and a duration where only that does.
dtcalc> now - 12:15
2026-05-23T00:00:13-04:00  America/New_York
dtcalc> 12:15 * 2
24h30m
dtcalc> -12:15
-12h15m
dtcalc> # Both readings typecheck here, so the tie-break picks the clock reading.
dtcalc> 12:15 + 3h
2026-05-23T15:15:00-04:00  America/New_York
dtcalc> # The two explicit forms force a duration, and name the leading unit.
dtcalc> 12:15h
12h15m
dtcalc> 12:15m
12m15s
dtcalc> :12:15
12m15s
dtcalc> ::15
15s
dtcalc> 1:02:03
2026-05-23T01:02:03-04:00  America/New_York
dtcalc> 12:15:13.5 in Tokyo
2026-05-24T01:15:13.5+09:00  Asia/Tokyo
dtcalc> # An impossible clock reading is fine as a duration.
dtcalc> now + 25:00
2026-05-24T13:15:13-04:00  America/New_York
dtcalc> 25:00 in Tokyo
error: '25:00' is not a time of day
  25:00 in Tokyo
  ^^^^^
dtcalc> 
dtcalc> # two bare colon literals joined by + or - are ambiguous
dtcalc> 2:11 - 1:29
error: 2:11 - 1:29 is ambiguous: a time of day less a duration, or two durations
  2:11 - 1:29
  ^^^^^^^^^^^
  as a time of day and a duration: 2:11 - 1:29h
  as two durations (2h11m - 1h29m): 2:11h - 1:29
dtcalc> 2:11 + 1:29
error: 2:11 + 1:29 is ambiguous: a time of day plus a duration, or two durations
  2:11 + 1:29
  ^^^^^^^^^^^
  as a time of day and a duration: 2:11 + 1:29h
  as two durations (2h11m + 1h29m): 2:11h + 1:29
dtcalc> 2:11h - 1:29
42m
dtcalc> 2:11 - 1:29h
2026-05-23T00:42:00-04:00  America/New_York
